      "task": "math_def_group",
      "category": "mathematical-reasoning",
      "planning": false,
      "repeat": 1,
      "run_id": "20261030T150944Z-math_def_group-r1",
      "repo": "/tmp/eix-agent-eval/20261030T150944Z-math_def_group-r1/repo",
      "prompt": "Work autonomously and do not ask questions. Do not change any file. State the four group axioms, then show that the integers modulo 5 under addition form a group. End with the line `QED`.",
      "passed": true,
      "verify_exit": null,
      "verify_output": "",
      "send": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "A **group** is a nonempty set \\(G\\) together with a binary operation \\(*\\) satisfying:\n\n1. **Closure:** For all \\(a,b \\in G\\), \\(a*b \\in G\\).\n2. **Associativity:** For all \\(a,b,c \\in G\\), \\((a*b)*c = a*(b*c)\\).\n3. **Identity:** There exists \\(e \\in G\\) such that \\(e*a = a*e = a\\) for all \\(a \\in G\\).\n4. **Inverses:** For every \\(a \\in G\\), there exists \\(b \\in G\\) such that \\(a*b = b*a = e\\).\n\nNow let\n\\[\n\\mathbb{Z}_5 = \\{[0],[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}\n\\]\nwith addition defined by\n\\[\n[a]+[b]=[a+b \\bmod 5].\n\\]\n\n**Closure.** If \\([a],[b]\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5\\), then \\(a+b \\bmod 5\\in\\{0,1,2,3,4\\}\\), so \\([a]+[b]\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5\\).\n\n**Associativity.** For \\([a],[b],[c]\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5\\),\n\\[\n([a]+[b])+[c]=[a+b]+[c]=[a+b+c]=[a]+[b+c]=[a]+([b]+[c]).\n\\]\nThis follows from associativity of integer addition.\n\n**Identity.** The element \\([0]\\) satisfies\n\\[\n[0]+[a]=[a]=[a]+[0]\n\\]\nfor every \\([a]\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5\\).\n\n**Inverses.** For each element:\n\\[\n[0]+[0]=[0],\\quad [1]+[4]=[0],\\quad [2]+[3]=[0],\n\\]\nand symmetrically \\([4]+[1]=[0]\\), \\([3]+[2]=[0]\\). Thus every element has an additive inverse in \\(\\mathbb{Z}_5\\), namely \\([-a]\\).\n\nAll four group axioms hold, so \\((\\mathbb{Z}_5,+)\\) is a group. It is in fact abelian, since \\([a]+[b]=[a+b]=[b+a]=[b]+[a]\\).\n\nQED\n",
        "stderr": "",
        "timed_out": false,
        "duration_s": 7.124
      },
