    {
      "task": "math_theorem_rolle",
      "category": "mathematical-reasoning",
      "planning": false,
      "repeat": 1,
      "run_id": "20261030T150951Z-math_theorem_rolle-r1",
      "repo": "/tmp/eix-agent-eval/20261030T150951Z-math_theorem_rolle-r1/repo",
      "prompt": "Work autonomously and do not ask questions. Do not change any file. State Rolle's theorem including all hypotheses. Verify the hypotheses for f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 3 on the interval [1, 3], then find the value c guaranteed by the theorem. End with the line `QED`.",
      "passed": true,
      "verify_exit": null,
      "verify_output": "",
      "send": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "**Rolle's Theorem.** If \\(f\\) satisfies:\n\n1. \\(f\\) is continuous on the closed interval \\([a,b]\\),\n2. \\(f\\) is differentiable on the open interval \\((a,b)\\),\n3. \\(f(a)=f(b)\\),\n\nthen there exists at least one \\(c \\in (a,b)\\) such that \\(f'(c)=0\\).\n\n**Verification for \\(f(x)=x^{2}-4x+3\\) on \\([1,3]\\).**\n\n1. *Continuity:* \\(f\\) is a polynomial, hence continuous on all of \\(\\mathbb{R}\\), in particular on \\([1,3]\\).\n2. *Differentiability:* \\(f'(x)=2x-4\\) exists for every real \\(x\\), so \\(f\\) is differentiable on \\((1,3)\\).\n3. *Equal endpoint values:*\n   \\[\n   f(1)=1-4+3=0,\\qquad f(3)=9-12+3=0,\n   \\]\n   so \\(f(1)=f(3)=0\\).\n\nAll three hypotheses hold, so Rolle's theorem applies.\n\n**Finding \\(c\\).** Solve\n\\[\nf'(c)=2c-4=0 \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; c=2.\n\\]\nSince \\(2 \\in (1,3)\\), the guaranteed value is \\(c=2\\). Indeed \\(f(2)=4-8+3=-1\\), the vertex minimum of the parabola, where the tangent is horizontal.\n\nQED\n",
        "stderr": "",
        "timed_out": false,
        "duration_s": 4.622
      },
